Installed with the Yarn 4.16.0 binary shipped in the tag
(vendor/pdfkit/.yarn/releases/yarn-4.16.0.cjs). node_modules and the
rollup build under js/ are gitignored. Versions below are the ones
yarn.lock resolved.

fontkit            2.0.4    MIT, Devon Govett
linebreak          1.1.0    MIT, Devon Govett
png-js             2.0.0    MIT, Devon Govett
@noble/hashes      1.8.0    MIT
@noble/ciphers     1.3.0    MIT
fflate             0.8.3    MIT

Also present, because fontkit pulls them in:

restructure        3.0.2    MIT
unicode-properties 1.4.1    MIT

js-md5 is not a dependency of this tag. The August tree resolved
js-md5 0.8.3. md5.lua is a transcription of RFC 1321, not of that
package. PDFKit 0.20.2 imports MD5 from @noble/hashes.

png-js moved from 1.1.0 in the August tree to 2.0.0 here. The Lua
reader was re-read against the Node build, lib/png-js.js. That build
still inflates with zlib, and it still parses IHDR, PLTE, IDAT, tRNS,
tEXt, and IEND. The browser file png.js adds APNG chunks and uses
fflate. PDFKit imports the Node build, and png_reader.lua follows that
build. Family J matches 0.20.2.

fontkit 2.0.4, linebreak 1.1.0, @noble/hashes 1.8.0, and
@noble/ciphers 1.3.0 are the same versions the August tree resolved.

fflate is the browser deflate. The Node build still calls
zlib.deflateSync. The Lua compressor stays the zlib 1.3.1
transcription.
